@module gameturn ; the game turn: the clock, daily production, capture and the turn pacing
@about The second half of every pass of the play loop and of every robot menu loop: WorldTurn moves the robots and shots, GameTurn then keeps the time and the rules that are not a robot's.
@about In calling order: GameTurn steps Random and the clock (+5 minutes a turn; a new day runs DailyProduction, which runs ProduceSide and AddCapped for both sides); PrintInline prints the clock position and GameTurnEnd prints the days and HH.MM; CheckGameEnd (the endings module) ends the game when a side has no warbase; CaptureLoop counts the turns a robot stands on each of the 28 base doors and hands a base over at 144 (GiveWarbase / GiveFactory, then CountBases and UpdateStatusPanel); TurnPace waits until a turn has lasted 10 frames.
@about Data it owns or keeps: Clock ($FD35: minutes, hours, the 16-bit day count), TurnFrames ($FD34, counted up by PlayInterrupt), the capture counters (+4 of each 5-byte record in Warbases $FD70 / Factories $FD84), the resources of both sides (Resources, EnemyResources) through the building counts PlayerBuildings / EnemyBuildings.
@about Tricks: PrintInline reads the print codes after the CALL (ClockPos) and returns past them, so the code goes on behind the text. UnusedTapeCode is dead code between the routines.
$AD62 c GameTurn ; One game turn: the random step, the clock, the daily production, the clock print
> Random steps the random generator $FD00-$FD03. Clock ($FD35 minutes, $FD36 hours, $FD37-$FD38 days) gains 5 minutes a turn: 60 minutes make an hour, 24 hours a day, and a new day runs DailyProduction. Then the clock print: days at (0,27), five digits with leading spaces; "HH.MM" on the next line. Goes on in GameTurnEnd.
$AD68 ; the minutes
$AD69 ; + 5
$AD6B ; store
$AD6C ; 60 minutes?
$AD6E ; not yet: print
$AD72 ; HL = the hours
$AD73 ; one hour more
$AD74 ; the hours:
$AD75 ; 24?
$AD77 ; not yet: print
$AD7B ; the day count, 16 bits
$AD7E ; one day more
$AD7F ; store it
$AD62 ; the random generator
$AD65 ; 5 minutes a turn
$AD70 ; an hour
$AD79 ; a day
$AD82 ; the day's production of both sides
$AD85 ; position, setting 0, attribute $57
$AD88 t ClockPos ; The clock: (0,27), size 0, attribute $57
@res game/text/clock-pos.bin

$AD90 c GameTurnEnd ; Game turn, second half: the clock print, the game end, captures, the frame pacing
> The second half of GameTurn, reached after the PrintInline of ClockPos (setting the print position (0,27) and attribute $57). Prints the days (PrintNumber5, five digits with leading spaces) and, a line down (PrintNewline), the hours "." the minutes (PrintNumber2Zero, two digits with zeros). Then CheckGameEnd: a side with no warbase ends the game here.
> Captures: the 28 capture points at $FD70 (5 bytes each: X 2 bytes, Y, owner and type, count; points 0-3 the warbases, 4-27 the factories) are checked each turn. While map bit 6 is set on a point's door cell (an anchor stands there) its count +4 goes up; at 144 ($90) FindRobot takes the robot there and its side (+$0A bit 7) captures the building: GiveWarbase for a warbase, GiveFactory (point - 4) for a factory. A door anchor that is no robot (probably a flying shot) captures nothing; the count still starts again. An empty door resets the count. Any robot captures, whatever its order. After a capture CountBases recounts the buildings and UpdateStatusPanel reprints the status.
> Last, the pacing (TurnPace): waits until PlayInterrupt has counted 10 frames in TurnFrames ($FD34) since the last turn, then clears it. A turn is at least 10 frames: an hour 120, a game day 2880 (about 58 s). Keeps IY (pushed around the loop); A, BC, DE, HL lost.
