# --- the main menu
@module mainmenu ; the main menu, the disk load and save hooks, the redefine-keys screen, the dead tape code
@about What the player sees before a game: the menu picture (MenuPicture, drawn by bank 3's code), the six options 0..СТАРТ ИГРЫ to 5..ЗАГРУЗКА, the tune (MusicInterrupt), the redefine screen; key 5 loads a saved game from the disk (LoadGame -> GameLoad). In play the save key comes here too: PlayLoop jumps to SaveGameStage, which stages the shots and the buildings and goes on to GameSave.
@about Calling order: Restart ($A62A) calls MainMenu: ClearScreen, MenuPicture, the options (each option's colour from ControlsOptionAttr), MenuOptionsEnd, then MainMenuKeys: wait for all keys up, then a key a frame, KEY-SCAN and the ROM key table decide: 0 MenuStart (Z), 1-3 MenuSetControls (Controls, the options again), 4 RedefineKeys (then the whole menu), 5 LoadGame (no return: the game comes back through LoadReturn).
@about The menu does not use KeyTable or ReadControls: it reads the keyboard with the ROM's KEY-SCAN ($028E) and the ROM's key table ($0205), so 0-5 work whatever keys were defined. RedefineKeys clears and refills KeyTable (module controls) through DefineKey: a key value E becomes the 3-byte record (port high byte, bit mask, code) ReadControls reads.
@about Inline strings everywhere: a CALL PrintInline is followed by its text (position, attribute and size codes, then characters, 0), and execution goes on after the 0. PrintKeyPrompt ends in JP PrintInline, so the key name after each CALL PrintKeyPrompt is a string too; the checks for SYM SH / ENTER / CAPS SH / SPACE each put a RET after their name string (KeySpaceDone for SPACE, in the next byte). The names of SYMBOL SHIFT and ENTER are Latin letters the Russian font draws as ЯУМ ЯН and ЕНТЕР.
@about Dead code kept in the image: the tape load (LoadTapePrompt, LoadGameBlocks with its checksum test turned into NOPs, LoadBad, LoadError), the tape save's start (SaveGame, SaveGameBlocks' key wait) and its end (SaveTapeBlocks), and PrintTitle (NOPs). Their texts are translated too. Nothing jumps into them.
$C100 c MainMenu ; The main menu: clear the screen, the title, the options; Z = start a new game, NZ = a game was loaded
> Called by Restart ($A62A), which falls into NewGameSetup with Z when it returns; a loaded game never returns here (LoadReturn goes on to NewGameSetup with NZ). Clears the screen, draws the menu picture (MenuPicture: bank 3's code) and the options 0-5; the current controls (Controls, $D3E4) show in cyan, the others in yellow ($C336). Then MainMenuKeys. Keys 1-3 choose the controls and redraw the options, 4 redefines the keys and redraws the whole menu, 5 loads a saved game, 0 starts.
$C100 ; the menu starts on an empty black screen
$C106 c MainMenuOptions ; The main menu's options (re-entered after keys 1-3)
$C106 ; option 0, СТАРТ ИГРЫ (start game)
$C109 t MenuStartText ; "0..СТАРТ ИГРЫ" (start game) at (10,1), double height, yellow
@res game/text/menu-start.bin
> PrintInline codes: attribute $46, setting $21 (double height), position row 11 column 8, the text, setting $00.
