@module screen ; the play screen: its frame and colours, the status panel, screen-line steps, Random
@about The fixed parts of the play screen and the helpers every module uses. DrawPlayScreen draws it all once (at EnterPlay and after the construction menu): ClearScreen, DrawView, the frame of the view (22 x 22 characters from (0,0), double lines), the attributes ($07 all, $78 the frame, $70 the view, $71 / $41 the blue corner past the map's south edge) and PlayScreenText (ДЕНЬ:, ЧАС:, the tall РАДАР:).
@about The right panel, columns 22-31: ShowStatusPanel = ClearPanel + StatusPanelText (the labels); UpdateStatusPanel reprints the numbers (the Resources, both sides' building counts and robots) through PrintResourceValues, PrintInsgCounts, PrintHumnCounts and PrintHumnRobots, each the tail after an inline position string. PanelBusy = 1 (a robot menu prints there) stops it.
@about Helpers: DrawMaskedUp (masked pictures straight onto the screen, the construction menu), NextScreenLine / PrevScreenLine (the screen's line order), TableWord and AddAToHL (table lookups), and Random, the game's only random source (a 32-bit shift register in RandomSeed $FD00).
@about Inline data: every string here follows a CALL PrintInline (control codes 1 position, 2 attribute, 3 newline, 4 size, 0 end; see the print module), and the code goes on after its 0. The operand of LD (HL),A at $D371 (Random+$19) is self-modified: the index of the last byte Random returned.
$D0B9 c ClearScreen ; Clear the screen (pixels and attributes to 0) and make the border black
> Clears the 6912 bytes of pixels and attributes from $4000 and sets the border black (and the speaker off) with OUT ($FE),0. Called by DrawPlayScreen, MainMenu $C100, RedefineKeys $C34A and OpenConstructionMenu $C865. Changes A, BC, DE, HL.
