# ---- the endings, the main menu, the disk load and save, the font ----
@module endings ; the end of a game: Dead End or Final Cut, the AY silenced
@about CheckGameEnd runs once a game turn from GameTurn. When the enemy has no warbase left the game is won: GameWon copies the Final Cut block from bank 6 to $6060 and runs it. When we have none the game is lost: bank 3 is paged and its Dead End runs. Both silence the AY first (Silence), go back to IM 1 with I = $3F (the ROM's interrupt, the game's handlers no longer wanted) and never return; the machine is the ending's from then on.
@about What follows them is the old end of a game that nothing reaches any more: GameOverWait (the beep, 100 frames, a key, Restart) and GameStop (the panel and the menu handler; its handler write misses ImHandler). The gaps between the routines are zero bytes and the last 9 bytes of an old text line.
$AE6B c CheckGameEnd ; The end of the game: the enemy has no warbase (won) or we have none (lost)
> Called once a game turn by GameTurn. EnemyBuildings+0 = 0 (no enemy warbase): GameWon. Else PlayerBuildings+0 not 0: back to the turn. Else the game is lost: Silence, I = $3F, IM 1, EI, bank 3 ($13) and JP DeadEnd ($D2EF in bank 3). The lost path takes the CALL first only to empty the AY; nothing comes back.
$AE6B ; the enemy's warbases
$AE6F ; none left: won
$AE71 ; ours
$AE75 ; we still have one: play on
$AE76 ; lost: the tune off
$AE79 ; the ROM's I and IM 1: no game handler from here on
$AE80 ; bank 3: Dead End
$AE87 ; Dead End's entry, never back
$AE8A s EndingsSpare1 ; 10 bytes, never used
$AE94 c Silence ; The AY's registers 0-14 to zero: no tone, no noise, volume 0 on all three channels
> Waits for one interrupt first (HALT), so the music handler has played its last frame, then turns interrupts off for good: the endings set their own. A counts the registers; each is selected at $FFFD and written 0 at $BFFD.
$AE95 ; the last frame of the tune
$AE96 ; no more handlers
$AE97 SilenceRegister ; select register A
$AE9D ; write 0 to it
$AEA3 ; the next register, up to 14
$AEA9 s EndingsSpare2 ; 8 bytes, never used
$AEB1 c GameWon ; The enemy has no warbase left: the Final Cut block from bank 6 to $6060, and run
> Silence, I = $3F, IM 1, EI, bank 6 ($16), $3637 bytes from FinalCutBlock ($C000 in bank 6) copied to FinalCut ($6060, over the view buffer, the sprites and the code past it), bank 0 again and JP FinalCut: the block unpacks and plays the ending and never returns.
$AEB1 ; the tune off
$AEB4 ; the ROM's I and IM 1
$AEBB ; bank 6: the Final Cut block
$AEC2 ; from bank 6's start
$AEC8 ; the block's bytes
$AECB ; copied over the game itself
$AECD ; bank 0 at $C000 again
$AED4 ; the Final Cut block's start
$AED7 s EndingsSpare3 ; 10 bytes, never used
$AEE1 b OldEndText ; The last 9 bytes of an old end-of-game text line: 8 spaces and its 0, never read
$AEEA c GameOverWait ; Code nothing reaches: the old end of a game, a beep, a pause, a key, Restart
> Both ends of a game leave the game now, so no path comes here. The code: the beep with A = $FA, 100 frames of HALT, WaitRelease, then WaitKey until a control is held and JP Restart.
$AEF1 GameOverPause ; 100 frames of HALT before the key is read
$AEF7 GameOverKey ; wait for a key, then back to Restart
$AF00 c GameStop ; Code nothing calls: give the panel back to the status, the menu handler
> PanelBusy = 0, ClearPanel, ShowStatusPanel, then LD HL,MusicInterrupt and LD ($6D6A),HL: a typo for ImHandler ($696A). Run, it would write the handler's address into the sprites ($6D6A) and leave the interrupt as it was. No CALL GameStop is left in the game.
$AF0D ; meant for ImHandler: $6D6A is a byte of the sprites

$C103 c MainMenuTitle ; The main menu without the clearing: the picture, then the options
$C103 ; the menu picture from bank 3
$C192 c MainMenuKeys ; The main menu's keys: wait for all keys up, then a key 0-5
> Waits until no key is held (KEY-SCAN $028E), then reads a key every frame (one HALT a pass; the tune plays from MusicInterrupt meanwhile) and takes its character from the ROM's key table ($0205): 0 returns Z, 1-3 set Controls and redraw the options, 4 RedefineKeys then the whole menu, 5 LoadGame. Any other key is ignored. The NOPs are 4 + 3 + 3 zero bytes where calls stood: the wait loops have nothing else to do.
$C192 ; wait until no key is held
$C196 ; ROM KEY-SCAN: E = the key value, $FF none
$C199 ; E bit 7 set: no key
$C19A ; sets S from bit 7
$C19B ; a key still held (from the last choice): wait
$C1A1 MenuWaitKey ; one frame a pass
$C1A5 ; ROM KEY-SCAN
$C1A8 ; E = $FF: no key
$C1A9 ; sets S from bit 7
$C1AA ; none yet: wait
$C1AD ; the key's character from the ROM's main key table
$C1B0 ; $0205 + E (no carry: E is at most $27)
$C1B1 ; L = $05 + E
$C1B2 ; A = the key's character
$C1B3 ; "5"?
$C1B5 ; 5: load a saved game from the disk
$C1B7 ; "0"?
$C1B9 ; 0: start
$C1BB ; "1"?
$C1BD ; 1: keyboard
$C1BF ; "2"?
$C1C1 ; 2: Kempston
$C1C3 ; "3"?
$C1C5 ; 3: Interface 2
$C1C7 ; "4"?
$C1C9 ; any other key: ignored, wait again
$C1CB ; 4: redefine the keys, then the whole menu again
$C1CE ; the whole menu again (clear, picture, options, keys)
$C1D1 MenuStart ; Z: a new game
$C1D2 ; Z: Restart goes on into NewGameSetup ($A62D)
$C1D3 MenuKeyboard ; 1: keyboard
$C1D5 ; Controls = 1
$C1D7 MenuKempston ; 2: Kempston
$C1D9 ; Controls = 2
$C1DB MenuInterface2 ; 3: Interface 2
$C1DD MenuSetControls ; Controls, then the options again
$C1E0 ; reprint the options in the new colours, then the keys
$C18B c MenuOptionsEnd ; The options' last step after their text: one frame, then MainMenuKeys
> PrintInline returns here past the 0 of MenuMoreText: a HALT and 6 NOPs (zero bytes where a longer text ended), on into MainMenuKeys.
$C1E3 c PrintTitle ; Code nothing calls: 25 NOPs and a RET
> 25 zero bytes and the RET, where a title print stood; the menu's title is in MenuPicture's picture.
$C1FD c LoadGame ; Key 5: load a saved game from the disk (GameLoad)
$C200 c LoadTapePrompt ; Code nothing reaches: the PlayTapeText prompt, then on into LoadGameBlocks
> Left behind the JP of LoadGame. It prints its inline text and would fall into the tape load LoadGameBlocks.

$C21E c LoadGameBlocks ; Code nothing reaches: the tape load of a saved game, its checksum test gone
> The tape load, left in the image: red border, two headerless blocks (flag $00) through the ROM's LD-BYTES past its border set-up ($0562): 2 bytes to $5B00, then $24D1 bytes to $D92B-$FDFB; then SaveChecksum, and 10 NOPs where the comparison with the loaded sum stood, so the load would count as good: the first 45 bytes back to Shots, the next 168 to Buildings, NZ. LoadGame jumps to the disk load instead; nothing comes here.
$C21E ; red border while it loads
$C220 ; border red ($02)
$C222 ; 2 bytes: the checksum
$C226 ; DE = 2 bytes
$C229 ; flag $00, carry set: load
$C22A ; carry set: LOAD, not VERIFY
$C22B ; INC D / DEC D with the flags saved between: NZ in AF' as LD-BYTES wants
$C22C ; AF' = flag $00, load
$C22D ; D back to 0
$C22E ; LD-BYTES runs with interrupts off
$C22F ; ROM LD-BYTES past its border set-up and the SA/LD-RET push
$C232 ; the game block
$C236 ; DE = $24D1 bytes: $D92B-$FDFB
$C23F ; ROM LD-BYTES: the robots, the map, the variables, the staged shots and buildings
$C242 ; border black again
$C245 ; DE = the block's sum
$C248 ; 10 NOPs: no comparison, every load is good
$C252 ; the staged tables back to their places
$C255 ; the 5 records of 9 bytes at Shots
$C25D ; the buildings
$C265 ; LD-BYTES left interrupts off
$C266 ; NZ: a game was loaded
$C269 c LoadBad ; Code nothing reaches: ОШИБКА ВВОДА (load error), its text inline, then LoadError
> The tape load's error branch; the test that jumped here is gone (LoadGameBlocks' NOPs).
$C282 c LoadError ; Code nothing reaches: after the load error, a beep, a key, then Restart
> Beep with A = $FA, WaitAnyKey, then JP Restart. Reached only from LoadBad.
$C282 ; the error beep: half-period delay $FA
$C287 ; a key to go on
$C28A ; the whole start-up again, then the menu
$C28D c SaveGame ; Code nothing reaches: the menu handler, the tape prompt, then SaveGameBlocks
> The tape save's start, left in the image: ImHandler = MusicInterrupt, the inline RecordText prompt at row 22, and on into SaveGameBlocks' key wait. PlayLoop's save key jumps past all of it to SaveGameStage.
$C28D ; the menu handler: the music plays, the play handler stops
$C290 ; ImHandler
$C293 ; the prompt at row 22
$C2C9 c SaveGameBlocks ; Save the game: a key (the unused part), the staging, then GameSave on the disk
> SaveGameBlocks itself (the key wait for the tape) is reached only from SaveGame, which nothing runs. PlayLoop's save key enters at SaveGameStage ($C2CC): RadarDirty = 1 (the staging overwrites the radar picture past RadarEnemy), the 45 bytes of Shots to SaveShots ($D92B) and the 168 of Buildings to SaveBuildings ($D958), so $D92B-$FDFB holds the whole game; interrupts off and JP GameSave, which comes back to PlayLoop's JP EnterPlay.
$C2C9 ; the tape's key wait (not reached)
$C2CC SaveGameStage ; the save key in play (PlayLoop $A71A) enters here
$C2CE ; RadarDirty: the staging below overwrites the tail of RadarEnemy
$C2D4 ; to SaveShots
$C2D7 ; 45 bytes
$C2DA ; Shots -> SaveShots; DE now SaveBuildings
$C2DF ; 168 bytes
$C2E2 ; Buildings -> SaveBuildings: $D92B-$FDFB is now the whole game
$C2E4 ; interrupts off: GameSave turns them on for its HALT
$C2E5 ; the disk save in bank 4
$C2E8 s SaveSpare ; 14 zero bytes where the start of the tape save stood
$C2F6 c SaveTapeBlocks ; Code nothing reaches: the rest of the old tape save, two ROM SA-BYTES calls
> XOR A; SCF; CALL $04D0 (the first block, its set-up gone with the zero bytes before it), then $24D1 bytes from SaveShots with flag $00, border black, EI. Nothing jumps here.
$C2F6 ; flag $00
$C2F8 ; ROM SA-BYTES past its pilot choice: HL = the pilot, A = the flag
$C2FE ; from SaveShots ...
$C302 ; ... $24D1 bytes, to $FDFB
$C307 ; ROM SA-BYTES: the game block

$C4A0 t KeyNameSpace ; "ПРОБЕЛ" (space)
@res game/text/key-name-space.bin
$C4A7 c KeySpaceDone ; The end of DefineKey's SPACE branch: RET after its name string
> The SPACE name is one letter longer than the room it had, so its 0 ends on $C4A6 and its RET is this byte.

@module font ; the game's Cyrillic font and the free bytes round it
@about GameFont holds the 64 glyphs of codes $20-$5F, 8 bytes each from the top line; PrintChar and PrintBigChar read glyph code at $C400 + 8 x code (GameFont - $100). The game's letters are Russian drawn over the Latin codes (tools/game_text.py: a look-alike where there is one, a free code for the rest; $33 is both 3 and З).
@about Resource: src/res/game/gfx/font.png (16 glyphs a row). Before the font, $C4A8-$C4FF, and after it, $C700-$C848, are unused bytes up to ConstructionMenu: the $FE at $C4A8 and zeros.
$C4A8 b FontSpare1 8 ; 88 bytes, never used: a $FE, then zeros
$C500 b GameFont 8 ; The font: 64 glyphs of 8 bytes, codes $20-$5F, the Russian letters over the Latin ones
@res game/gfx/font.bin
> Read by PrintChar ($D4B7) and PrintBigChar ($D4E0) only. Zero-based on code $20, the space.
$C700 s FontSpare2 ; 329 bytes, never used, up to ConstructionMenu

# The work space past the loaded image ($FD00-$FFFF): docs/02-architecture.md
@equ $FD00 RandomSeed 4 ; the shift register of Random, seeded $39,$30,$39,$30 by Restart
@equ $FD04 PrintAddr 2 ; the screen address of the next printed character
@equ $FD06 MapView 2 ; the map byte at the view's left column: $DD00 + ViewX
@equ $FD08 SavedSP 2 ; SP kept while ClearViewBuffer pushes and while the menu music runs
@equ $FD0A ViewX 2 ; the map column at the view's left edge, follows ShipX
@equ $FD0C Input ; the controls read this game turn: bit 0 right, 1 left, 2 down, 3 up, 4 fire, 5 save, 6 abort, 7 pause
@equ $FD0D ShipY ; the ship's row, 1-15
@equ $FD0E ShipX 2 ; the ship's column, $000E-$01F5
@equ $FD10 Altitude ; the ship's height: fire raises it by 2 to $30, released it sinks by 1 to what is under it
@equ $FD11 ShipDrawPos 2 ; the ship's view position while its drawing is deferred (column, row); 0 = not deferred
@equ $FD13 PrintAttr ; the attribute of printed characters
@equ $FD14 PrintAttrAddr 2 ; the attribute address of the next printed character
@equ $FD16 PrintHeight ; big characters: each font row printed this many times (PrintInline code 4, high nibble)
@equ $FD17 PrintWidth ; big characters: the width in bytes, 0 normal (PrintInline code 4, low nibble)
@equ $FD1A RadarPhase ; toggled each frame: 0 shows the player's radar layer, 1 the enemy's
@equ $FD1B RadarLeft ; the radar window's left edge in units of 8 map columns, 0-$30
@equ $FD1C RadarColumn 2 ; RadarLeft x 8: the radar window's first map column
@equ $FD1E RadarBlink ; bit 0: the ship's radar blip is drawn
@equ $FD1F MenuCursor 2 ; the construction menu: the column (0 ВЫХОД, 1 ВЫПУСК, 2 the parts), the part row; the robot menu: its last item
@equ $FD21 MenuParts ; the parts chosen, bit = part row; the new robot's +$07
@equ $FD22 Resources 7 ; general, electronics, nuclear, phasers, missiles, cannon, chassis
@equ $FD29 MenuResources 7 ; the copy the construction menu spends; back to Resources on ВЫПУСК (start the robot)
@equ $FD30 ClimbTurns ; game turns the ship still climbs by itself: 3 at a new game, 5 after a menu
@equ $FD31 PrintColumn ; the print position's column
@equ $FD32 PrintRow ; the print position's row
@equ $FD34 TurnFrames ; frames counted by PlayInterrupt; a game turn waits for 10
@equ $FD35 Clock 4 ; minutes (by 5), hours, days (16 bits)
@equ $FD39 PanelBusy ; 1 while a robot menu owns the right panel
@equ $FD3A PlayerBuildings 7 ; the player's buildings by type: warbases, then factories in the Resources order
@equ $FD41 PlayerRobotCount ; live robots in slots 0-23
@equ $FD42 EnemyBuildings 7 ; the enemy's buildings, the same order; no warbase left = the game is won
@equ $FD49 EnemyRobotCount ; live robots in slots 24-47
@equ $FD4A EnemyResources 7 ; the enemy's resources, the order of Resources
@equ $FD51 Side ; the side being processed: 0 the player's, 1 the enemy's
@equ $FD52 RadarDirty ; 1: rebuild the radar layers from the map at the next ship mark
@equ $FD53 SoundFx ; 1-$7F a falling tone (fire), $FC a miss, $FA a hit, $C8 a robot destroyed; PlayInterrupt counts it on
@equ $FD70 Warbases 20 ; 4 capture points of 5 bytes: X (2), Y, owner (bit 6 player, 5 enemy, 7 destroyed) + type, turns a robot has stood at the door (144 captures)
@equ $FD84 Factories 120 ; 24 capture points of 5 bytes, the same shape
@equ $FF01 Buildings 168 ; 56 records of 3 bytes: the map cell address, the type (0 a warbase pad, 1-6 factories, 7 the player's flag, 8 the enemy's)
@isub $D401 LD BC,-100


# Inner branch labels
$A83B ShowStrengthNumber ; A = the strength (0 for a dying robot): three digits, leading spaces, then "%"
$AA70 DistanceLoop ; a game turn under the open menu, then WaitKey: fire sets, down / up step the miles
$AAB8 DistanceFire ; fire: +$0E = miles x 2; 0 miles turns the order back into 0 (stop)
$AAC4 DistanceDone ; the beep, WaitRelease, back to the robot menu
$AC81 CombatMenuLoop ; the combat list menu, A the highlighted item; 6 EXIT, 5 direct control, else a weapon
$AC99 CombatWeapon ; a weapon item: shift its part bit of +$07 into carry
$AC9F CombatPartBit ; rotate +$07 item + 1 times: carry = the robot has the weapon
$ACB3 CombatFireShot ; cannon / missiles / phasers: fire only when shot record 0 is free, then a turn
$ACCE CombatRefused ; no such weapon or the shot still flies: the refusal beep, back to the menu
$AD42 PaintMenuItemRow ; HL += 3 attribute rows, A times: item A's top row
$AD85 ClockPrint ; print the clock (also when no minute wrapped)
$ADFE CaptureFactory ; a point 4-27: factory A - 4 changes side
$AE04 CapturePointDone ; restore the capture count, on to the next point
$AE58 ProduceFactoryLoop ; each factory kind: 2 x its factories into its resource
$AE69 AddCappedStore ; store the capped sum
$AF3F ShipStepLeft ; one column left
$AF42 ShipCheckRight ; right: refused at column $1F5
$AF4B ShipStepRight ; one column right
$AF4C ShipCheckX ; the new column: refused when the ship would stand lower than what is there
$AF67 ViewCheckRight ; the ship at view column 22: the view one column right
$AF6C ViewStore ; ViewX and MapView = $DD00 + ViewX
$AF8C ShipCheckUp ; up: Y - 1
$AF90 ShipCheckY ; the new row: 0 / 16 off the map, CheckShipMove refuses a too low ship
$AFAE ClimbByFire ; no forced climb: fire climbs, else the ship sinks
$AFFF RadarScrollLeft ; the ship within 2 units of the window's left edge: the window 8 units left
$B084 ShipCompareTop ; carry: the ship's altitude below the highest top in C
$B0AF KeepHigherDone ; C is the bigger height
$B22B SteerMoveOrders ; orders 1-8: advance / retreat, destroy robots, the building orders
$B2B8 SteerNewBuilding ; another target building found: +$0E = its index
$B2E8 RobotAimCheck ; D = the wanted directions: 0 means on the target
$B2F9 RobotFaceDown ; on the target: face down and stand (destroy orders blast first)
$B306 RobotAimMove ; off the target: L = |the column difference|
$B30E RobotAimColumns ; 8 or more columns away: lean horizontally, else pick among the free wanted directions
$B381 ConsiderBuildingStart ; IY = the side's 24 robot records
$B395 ConsiderBuildingNext ; the next 16-byte robot record
$B3C3 KeepNearestNew ; nearer: BC = the new best distance, D = its index
$B3C8 KeepNearestDone ; back to the main registers
$B3E2 TargetWarbaseTable ; orders 5 and 8: the 4 warbase records
$B3E7 TargetBuildingMark ; E = the owner mark wanted: the opponent's
$B3F2 TargetNeutralCheck ; order 6 (capture neutral): mark 0
$B405 TargetRobotIndex ; HL = DE + 16 x (+$0E)
$B430 FindOpponentStart ; IY = the opponent's 24 records
$B441 FindOpponentNext ; the next 16-byte record, C its index
$B45C DirectStepSet ; C = the pushed direction (masked by the free ones when it faces it)
$B467 DirectStepStore ; +$05 and Input = the step, then RobotMove
$B486 TurnCheckVertical ; down <-> up: turn right / left first
$B48E TurnFace ; +$08 = the new facing, +$06 counts the turn
$B4C7 StepLeft ; left: column - 1, the distance order counted the other way
$B4D5 StepDown ; down: row + 1
$B4DA StepUp ; up: row - 1
$B532 FreeDirRight ; D = the terrain limit of the locomotion; right free?
$B53B FreeDirLeft ; left free?
$B544 FreeDirDown ; down free?
$B54D FreeDirUp ; up free?
$B556 FreeDirDone ; C = the free directions
$B605 SetStepDelayFind ; C = the ground class (0 flat, 3 low, 6 high); find the locomotion part
$B644 SpotEnemiesThree ; B = the range; three lanes, columns for down / up, rows for right / left
$B6C7 FindFreeShotSlot ; IY = the side's first shot record; Z when free, else the second
$B6E1 FireShotElectronics ; electronics: the range one step more
$B6E8 FireShotStart ; +$06 the range, +$05 the robot's facing, +$08 the wall height, the first step
$B70C FireShotDone ; the shot ended at once: MoveShot's miss / hit sound stays
$B72E MoveShotLeft ; left: 2 columns
$B735 MoveShotDown ; down: 2 rows
$B73C MoveShotUp ; up: 2 rows
$B741 MoveShotRows ; past the map's rows: the shot is gone
$B7D7 MoveShotKill ; strength 0 or less: dying for 4 turns, the explosion sound
$B7DB MoveShotStrength ; +$0C = the strength left
$BBC7 SetBaseOwnerBits ; the owner bit into the base's type byte
$BC6B RemoveBuildingDone ; restore BC, IY
$C31F ChecksumNext ; carry added into D; the next byte
$CC30 PartRowPaint ; paint the part's 4 x 3 cells in attribute E
$CC34 PartRowLine ; one attribute row of the part's 4 cells
$CC65 PreviewByteLoop ; copy B bytes of the buffer row to the screen line
$CD01 DiagonalNext ; the next cell down the diagonal
$CD2B DrawCellObjects ; then the object (bit 6) and the ship (bit 7)
$CD63 ShipCompareLatest ; is the latest object cell the ship's own? Then draw it now, else defer
$CDA7 FindLatestSameRow ; the cells (x-1, y) through (x+1, y+1)
$CDD5 KeepLaterTake ; HL is later: DE = HL
$CDE9 FindRobotNext ; the next 16-byte robot record
$CE06 FindBuildingNext ; the next 3-byte building record
$CE2E ShotSearchNext ; the next 9-byte shot record
$CE9C MoverRestore ; deferred: the record back to its real cell, the mark cleared
$CEBD MoverDrawReal ; at the real row: draw the sprite there
$CF6C ClipBottomSkip ; skip the sprite row's bytes
$CFD2 SpriteRowNext ; the next sprite row
$D0B4 CopyCharRowNext ; the next character row
$D109 FrameCornerTopLeft ; $80 down 6 lines at $4100: the top left corner of the double lines
$D113 FrameCornerTopRight ; $01 down 6 lines at $4115
$D11D FrameCornerBottomLeft ; $80 down 7 lines at $50A0
$D127 FrameCornerBottomRight ; $01 down 7 lines at $50B5
$D131 FrameSideLeft ; $81 down 162 lines at column 0
$D13D FrameSideRight ; $81 down 162 lines at column 21
$D170 FrameAttrSides ; attribute $78 at columns 0 and 21 of 20 rows
$D186 ViewAttrRow ; a row of 20 view cells
$D187 ViewAttrCell ; attribute $70
$D19A BlueCornerLoop ; 2 cells of $71 a row, 4 rows from $5A33
$D1B3 BlueEdgeRow1 ; 4 cells of $41 at $5A71
$D1BD BlueEdgeRow2 ; 6 cells of $41 at $5A8F
$D399 KeyShift ; the key's state (carry 1 pressed) into C
$D424 DigitPrint ; a digit: no more leading zeros, print "0" + A
$D43A PrintInlineEnd ; 0: return past the string
$D585 InterruptSound ; PlayMusic comes back here: the sound effect, the exit
$D582 InterruptRadar ; show this frame's radar picture
$D591 InterruptSoundStore ; SoundFx = the count, the effect's next step
$D598 InterruptExit ; restore the registers, on into EI; RET
$D651 RadarRobotNext ; the next 16-byte robot record
$D667 RadarDotRight ; the right pixel, maybe in the next byte
$D679 RadarDotAboveRight ; the right pixel of the line above
$D6A2 RadarMaskShift ; $80 shifted right (x AND 7) times
$D6A6 RadarDotOutside ; outside the window: return from ToggleRadarDot too

# Constants the image cannot tell from addresses
@isub $BA0A LD DE,-$0804
@isub $D4B7 LD DE,GameFont-$100
@isub $D4E0 LD DE,GameFont-$100

# The ROM's system variables the disk bridges set
@equ $5C08 LAST_K ; the ROM's last key: ENTER for the disk module
@equ $5C3B FLAGS ; the ROM's flags: $CC for the disk module's key reading
@equ $5C6A FLAGS2 ; the ROM's flags 2: bit 3 CAPS LOCK, cleared for the disk module

# The game's memory past the image (built at run time, zero or not loaded): the view buffer, the shots, the radar,
# the save staging, the robots, the map
@equ $5B00 ViewBuffer 3121 ; the view's back buffer, $5B00-$677F (160 lines of 20 bytes); its last 79 bytes are ViewBufferTail in the image
@equ $D7D3 Shots 45 ; the shots in flight: 5 records of 9 bytes; the block's last 5 bytes (zero) are its first
@equ $D800 RadarOwn 256 ; the radar picture with the player's robots: 16 lines of 16 bytes
@equ $D900 RadarEnemy 43 ; the radar picture with the enemy's robots, 16 lines of 16 bytes; SaveShots overlays its tail
@equ $D92B SaveShots 45 ; the save staging: the 5 Shots records (over RadarEnemy's tail)
@equ $D958 SaveBuildings 168 ; the save staging: the 56 Buildings records
@equ $DA00 Robots 384 ; the player's robots: slots 0-23, 16 bytes a record
@equ $DB80 EnemyRobots 384 ; the enemy's robots: slots 24-47, the same records
@equ $DD00 Map 8192 ; the map: 16 rows of 512 cells, cell = $DD00 + $200 x Y + X

# Addresses in the other banks (tools/game_mkgame.py turns these into EQU lines; the instructions name them by @isub)
# @bank $C000 PlayerInit 1 ; the SoundTrack player's start: the tune from its beginning
# @bank $C005 PlayerFrame 1 ; the player's frame entry: one 50 Hz step of the tune
# @bank $D8E1 MusicStart 1 ; bank 1's start-up code, run once by GameEntry
# @bank $C000 DiskModule 4 ; the disk module's entry; IX selects the job
# @bank $4000 DiskLoad 4 ; IX for the disk module: load a saved game
# @bank $4033 DiskSave 4 ; IX for the disk module: save the game
# @bank $D2EF DeadEnd 3 ; the lost game's ending
# @bank $E73B MenuPictureCode 3 ; the menu picture's depacker: the picture onto the screen
# @bank $C000 FinalCutBlock 6 ; the won game's ending, a block GameWon copies to FinalCut
# @bank $6060 FinalCut 6 ; where GameWon copies the Final Cut block and runs it (over the game)

# Instructions written with names the image cannot tell
@isub $6796 CALL PlayerFrame
@isub $67C3 CALL PlayerFrame
@isub $67E9 LD SP,GlueStack+73
@isub $67F1 CALL MenuPictureCode
@isub $6909 LD SP,GlueStack+73
@isub $690C LD IX,DiskSave
@isub $6928 JP DiskModule
@isub $A56E LD SP,GlueStack+73
@isub $A571 LD IX,DiskLoad
@isub $A58D JP DiskModule
@isub $A5E5 CALL MusicStart
@isub $A5FA CALL PlayerInit
@isub $AE87 JP DeadEnd
@isub $AEC2 LD HL,FinalCutBlock
@isub $AEC5 LD DE,FinalCut
@isub $AED4 JP FinalCut
@isub $AF0D LD ($6D6A),HL
@isub $D002 LD SP,ViewBuffer+3200
